Name: adblock-rust (Lumie C ABI integration)
Short Name: adblock-rust
URL: https://github.com/brave/adblock-rust
Version: 0.13.3
Revision: 886d45dcf5283ce8eddc6d961e7dd27966ab23f2
License: MPL-2.0
License File: LICENSE
Security Critical: yes
Shipped: yes

The upstream crate is pinned in Cargo.lock, with all dependency versions and
registry SHA256 checksums. vendor.tar.gz is an unmodified `cargo vendor --locked`
source snapshot including each dependency's license and checksum manifest.
The bridge src/lib.rs is maintained here; upstream code is unmodified.

Build with Rust 1.96.1 and OHOS SDK clang. build.py consumes the vendor archive
with --frozen --offline; no dependency resolution or download occurs in Ninja.
A separate liblumie_adblock.so isolates Rust allocation/runtime symbols from
Chromium's independently built Rust dependencies. It is loaded only in the browser
process using a C ABI. Immutable snapshots are matched on a sequenced worker.

Features: embedded-domain-resolver, full-regex-handling, css-validation.
The upstream single-thread feature is disabled. No resource-assembler, scriptlet
or redirect resource pack is shipped. See docs/OHOS_ADBLOCK.md for integration
boundaries and validation.

Bundled filter lists are independent copyrighted data, with their original
headers retained. lists/SOURCES.json records exact SHA256 snapshots and URLs.
Their licenses and attribution are in lists/NOTICE.md and accompanying texts.
